WEBVTT
X-TIMESTAMP-MAP=LOCAL:00:00:00.000,MPEGTS:0

00:00.797 --> 00:02.599 align:center line:81%
A little over a year ago,

00:02.633 --> 00:06.537 align:center line:79%
I was released from my assignment
in the Presidency of the Seventy,

00:06.537 --> 00:09.506 align:center line:79%
a change announced here
at the general conference.

00:09.506 --> 00:14.077 align:center line:79%
Because my name was read near those of
general authorities becoming emeritus,

00:14.244 --> 00:17.414 align:center line:79%
many assumed I also
finished my time of service.

00:18.682 --> 00:22.019 align:center line:79%
After the conference,
I received numerous messages of gratitude

00:22.019 --> 00:24.588 align:center line:81%
and good wishes for my next phase in life.

00:25.522 --> 00:28.492 align:center line:79%
Some even offered to buy my house
in North Salt Lake.

00:30.527 --> 00:32.529 align:center line:81%
It was nice to see that I would not ...

00:32.529 --> 00:37.000 align:center line:79%
I would be missed and also to know
we will not have trouble selling our home

00:37.000 --> 00:39.937 align:center line:81%
when I'm done. But I'm not there yet.

00:41.271 --> 00:44.641 align:center line:79%
My new assignment took Monica and me
to beautiful Africa,

00:44.975 --> 00:46.777 align:center line:81%
where the Church is flourishing.

00:47.311 --> 00:50.080 align:center line:79%
It has been a blessing to serve
among the faithful Saints

00:50.080 --> 00:55.018 align:center line:79%
in the Africa South Area and witness
the Lord’s love for them.

00:55.519 --> 00:59.489 align:center line:79%
It is inspiring to see
generational families of all backgrounds,

00:59.489 --> 01:04.194 align:center line:79%
including many successful
and well-educated Church members,

01:04.194 --> 01:07.197 align:center line:79%
dedicating their time
and talents to serve others.

01:08.565 --> 01:11.134 align:center line:79%
At the same time, given
the region’s demographics,

01:11.134 --> 01:14.071 align:center line:79%
many people of modest
means are joining the Church

01:14.071 --> 01:18.308 align:center line:79%
and transforming their lives through
the blessings of tithing faithfulness

01:18.408 --> 01:21.578 align:center line:79%
and the educational
opportunities offered by the Church.

01:22.646 --> 01:27.084 align:center line:79%
Programs such as Succeed in School,
EnglishConnect, BYU–Pathway,

01:27.284 --> 01:29.152 align:center line:81%
and the Perpetual Educational Fund

01:29.186 --> 01:33.056 align:center line:79%
bless many lives, especially
those of the rising generation.

01:34.024 --> 01:37.260 align:center line:81%
President James E. Faust once stated,

01:37.995 --> 01:42.499 align:center line:79%
“It has been said that this Church does
not necessarily attract great people,

01:43.166 --> 01:46.003 align:center line:79%
but more often makes
ordinary people great.”

01:47.270 --> 01:51.608 align:center line:81%
The greatness of our Saints

01:51.608 --> 01:56.113 align:center line:79%
in Africa becomes even more
evident as they face life's challenges

01:56.113 --> 01:58.115 align:center line:81%
and the demands of a growing Church.

01:58.649 --> 02:02.019 align:center line:79%
They always approach it
with a positive attitude.

02:02.486 --> 02:06.523 align:center line:79%
They embody well the well-known
teaching from President Nelson:

02:07.357 --> 02:11.161 align:center line:79%
“The joy we feel has little
to do with the circumstances of our lives

02:11.161 --> 02:14.031 align:center line:79%
and everything to do
with the focus of our lives.

02:14.431 --> 02:18.635 align:center line:79%
When the focus of our lives
is in God’s plan of salvation ...

02:18.635 --> 02:21.471 align:center line:81%
and Jesus Christ and His gospel,

02:21.605 --> 02:27.744 align:center line:79%
we can feel joy regardless of what is
happening—or not happening—in our lives.”

02:29.246 --> 02:32.249 align:center line:81%
They find joy despite their challenges.

02:32.449 --> 02:36.953 align:center line:79%
They have learned that our relationship
with the Savior enables us

02:36.953 --> 02:41.958 align:center line:79%
to approach difficulties
with smiling faces and grateful hearts.

02:42.726 --> 02:46.697 align:center line:79%
Let me share some of my experiences
with these faithful Saints

02:46.697 --> 02:48.432 align:center line:81%
who illustrate this principle,

02:48.832 --> 02:50.967 align:center line:81%
starting with a Mozambique.

02:52.069 --> 02:54.671 align:center line:79%
A few months ago,
I presided over a stake conference

02:54.671 --> 02:58.475 align:center line:79%
for a one-year-old stake
that already had 10 units.

02:59.076 --> 03:02.145 align:center line:79%
More than 2,000 people
filled the small chapel

03:02.145 --> 03:05.882 align:center line:79%
and three tents that were
set up outside. The stake

03:05.882 --> 03:13.023 align:center line:79%
president is 31 years old, his wife 26,
and they have two small children.

03:13.356 --> 03:18.495 align:center line:79%
And he leads this growing and challenging
stake with no complaints,

03:18.528 --> 03:21.998 align:center line:81%
only a smiling face and a grateful heart.

03:23.066 --> 03:24.935 align:center line:81%
In an interview with the patriarch,

03:25.135 --> 03:28.138 align:center line:81%
I learned that his wife was seriously ill

03:28.905 --> 03:31.174 align:center line:81%
and he struggled to provide for her care.

03:31.908 --> 03:34.811 align:center line:79%
After addressing the issue
with the stake president,

03:34.878 --> 03:37.314 align:center line:81%
we gave her a priesthood blessing.

03:37.948 --> 03:40.417 align:center line:79%
I inquired of the patriarch
how many patriarchal

03:40.417 --> 03:42.786 align:center line:81%
blessings he gives, on average,

03:43.220 --> 03:44.621 align:center line:81%
“Eight to ten,” he said.

03:45.689 --> 03:50.727 align:center line:79%
I replied, “Per month?”
And he said, “Per week.”

03:51.228 --> 03:55.031 align:center line:79%
I counseled him that doing
that many per weekend was not wise.

03:55.265 --> 03:58.668 align:center line:79%
“Elder Godoy,” he said, “they
keep coming every week,

03:58.668 --> 04:03.974 align:center line:79%
including new members and many youth.”
And again, no complaints,

04:04.307 --> 04:07.511 align:center line:81%
only a smiling face and a grateful heart.

04:08.411 --> 04:13.216 align:center line:79%
After the Sunday evening session of stake
conference on my way to the hotel,

04:13.216 --> 04:17.487 align:center line:79%
I noticed people buying food
along the road late at night.

04:18.421 --> 04:22.425 align:center line:79%
I asked my driver why they are doing
it when it was so dark,

04:22.826 --> 04:24.194 align:center line:81%
rather than during the day.

04:24.828 --> 04:29.032 align:center line:79%
He responded that they were working
during the day to have the money

04:29.032 --> 04:31.067 align:center line:81%
to do it later. “Oh,

04:32.235 --> 04:34.905 align:center line:79%
they were working today,
to eat tomorrow,” I said. But

04:35.872 --> 04:41.545 align:center line:79%
he corrected me. “No, they were working
during the day to eat tonight.”

04:43.213 --> 04:47.784 align:center line:79%
I had hoped our members
might be in a better situation,

04:48.251 --> 04:52.422 align:center line:79%
but he confirmed that many faced
similar challenges in that part

04:52.422 --> 04:53.423 align:center line:81%
of the country.

04:54.624 --> 04:57.694 align:center line:79%
The next morning
during our Sunday session,

04:58.061 --> 05:01.198 align:center line:79%
newly aware
of their circumstances,

05:01.631 --> 05:05.268 align:center line:79%
I was even more moved
by their smiling faces

05:06.770 --> 05:07.904 align:center line:81%
and grateful hearts.

05:08.738 --> 05:09.739 align:center line:81%
Zambia.

05:11.107 --> 05:12.943 align:center line:81%
On the way to the Sunday meeting,

05:13.176 --> 05:18.348 align:center line:79%
the stake president and I saw a couple
walking along the road with a baby

05:18.582 --> 05:20.050 align:center line:81%
and two small children.

05:20.517 --> 05:22.252 align:center line:81%
We stopped to offer them a ride.

05:23.386 --> 05:25.722 align:center line:81%
They were surprised and delighted.

05:25.722 --> 05:29.326 align:center line:79%
When I asked how far they needed
to walk to the chapel,

05:29.492 --> 05:34.164 align:center line:79%
the father replied that it could take
45 minutes to an hour,

05:34.497 --> 05:36.933 align:center line:81%
depending on the children's pace.

05:37.901 --> 05:43.940 align:center line:79%
They face this journey back and forth
every Sunday with no complaints,

05:44.341 --> 05:47.677 align:center line:81%
only smiling faces and grateful hearts.

05:49.045 --> 05:50.046 align:center line:81%
Malawi.

05:51.648 --> 05:53.850 align:center line:81%
One Sunday before a stake conference,

05:53.850 --> 05:59.589 align:center line:79%
I visited two branches using
public schools as meetinghouses.

06:00.090 --> 06:04.761 align:center line:79%
I was shocked by the humble and modest
conditions of the buildings,

06:05.128 --> 06:07.764 align:center line:81%
which lacked even some basic amenities.

06:08.531 --> 06:10.800 align:center line:81%
As I met a few members there,

06:10.867 --> 06:13.770 align:center line:79%
I was ready to apologize
for the inadequate

06:13.770 --> 06:16.106 align:center line:81%
conditions of their meeting house.

06:16.373 --> 06:20.010 align:center line:79%
But they were happy
to have a nearby place together,

06:20.343 --> 06:22.846 align:center line:81%
avoiding the usual long walk.

06:23.179 --> 06:29.085 align:center line:79%
And again, there were no complaints,
only smiling faces and grateful hearts.

06:30.587 --> 06:31.588 align:center line:81%
Zimbabwe.

06:33.290 --> 06:35.358 align:center line:81%
Following a Saturday leadership training,

06:35.425 --> 06:40.530 align:center line:79%
the stake president took me
to Sunday services held in a rented house.

06:41.298 --> 06:44.668 align:center line:81%
There were 240 people in attendance.

06:45.168 --> 06:49.940 align:center line:79%
Then the bishop introduced 10
new members baptized that week.

06:51.141 --> 06:55.078 align:center line:79%
The congregation was spread
across across two small rooms,

06:55.545 --> 07:00.483 align:center line:79%
with some members also sitting
outside the building watching

07:00.483 --> 07:03.053 align:center line:81%
the meeting through windows and doors.

07:05.055 --> 07:10.694 align:center line:79%
There were no complaints, only
the smiling faces and grateful hearts.

07:12.228 --> 07:13.229 align:center line:81%
Lesotho.

07:14.331 --> 07:18.835 align:center line:79%
I visited this beautiful small country,
also known as the Mountain Kingdom,

07:19.636 --> 07:22.839 align:center line:79%
to see a Church district preparing
to become a stake.

07:23.673 --> 07:25.709 align:center line:81%
Following a Saturday of meetings,

07:25.709 --> 07:31.147 align:center line:79%
I attended Sunday services in one
of their branches in a rented house.

07:32.048 --> 07:37.320 align:center line:79%
The sacramental room was overflowing
with people standing outside the door

07:37.320 --> 07:38.488 align:center line:81%
to participate.

07:39.689 --> 07:42.792 align:center line:79%
I told the branch president
that he needed a bigger house.

07:43.760 --> 07:50.633 align:center line:79%
To my surprise, he informed me
that this was only half of his membership.

07:51.267 --> 07:57.273 align:center line:79%
The other half would attend a second
sacrament meeting after the second hour.

07:58.208 --> 08:00.577 align:center line:81%
And again, there were no complaints,

08:00.577 --> 08:04.014 align:center line:79%
only smiling
faces and grateful hearts.

08:05.715 --> 08:09.619 align:center line:79%
I returned to Lesotho
later due to a fatal

08:09.652 --> 08:12.689 align:center line:79%
traffic accident
involving several of our youth,

08:12.722 --> 08:16.192 align:center line:79%
already mentioned by
Elder Christofferson earlier.

08:16.793 --> 08:18.628 align:center line:81%
When I visited these families,

08:18.695 --> 08:19.963 align:center line:81%
the families and leaders,

08:19.963 --> 08:22.499 align:center line:81%
I expected a somber atmosphere.

08:22.999 --> 08:27.237 align:center line:79%
Instead, I encountered
strong and resilient Saints

08:27.437 --> 08:32.442 align:center line:79%
who were coping with the situation
in an uplifting and inspiring way.

08:34.210 --> 08:40.884 align:center line:79%
Anicia Nku, 14, a survivor
accident victim in this picture,

08:41.117 --> 08:44.287 align:center line:81%
illustrated it well in her own words:

08:45.522 --> 08:48.558 align:center line:81%
“Trust in Jesus and always look unto Him,

08:49.826 --> 08:52.529 align:center line:81%
because through Him you will find peace

08:52.996 --> 08:56.733 align:center line:79%
and He will help you
in the healing process.”

08:58.201 --> 09:02.639 align:center line:79%
These are just a few examples
where we see their positive attitude

09:02.839 --> 09:07.577 align:center line:79%
because they center their lives
in the gospel of Jesus Christ.

09:08.178 --> 09:11.081 align:center line:81%
They know where to find help and hope.

09:12.048 --> 09:16.486 align:center line:79%
Why can the Savior succor them and us
in any circumstances of our lives?

09:16.820 --> 09:18.988 align:center line:81%
The answer can be found in the scriptures.

09:19.189 --> 09:21.424 align:center line:81%
“And he shall go forth suffering

09:21.424 --> 09:24.594 align:center line:79%
pains and afflictions
and temptations of every kind ....

09:24.828 --> 09:27.297 align:center line:79%
And he will take upon
him their infirmities,

09:27.297 --> 09:29.566 align:center line:81%
that his bowels may be filled with mercy,

09:29.899 --> 09:34.270 align:center line:79%
... that he may know ... how to succor his
people according to their infirmities.”

09:34.270 --> 09:40.043 align:center line:79%
As Elder Bednar taught, there is no
physical pain, anguish, or weakness

09:40.143 --> 09:44.948 align:center line:79%
we can experience that the Savior
does not know. “You and I

09:45.348 --> 09:48.685 align:center line:81%
in a moment of weakness may cry out,

09:48.985 --> 09:52.155 align:center line:79%
’No one understands
[what I’m going through]. ...

09:52.188 --> 09:55.125 align:center line:81%
No human being, perhaps, knows.

09:55.125 --> 09:58.428 align:center line:79%
But the Son of God ...
perfectly knows and understands.”

09:59.028 --> 10:03.833 align:center line:79%
And why? Because “He felt and bore
our burdens before we ever did.”

10:04.167 --> 10:08.938 align:center line:79%
I conclude with my testimony
of Christ’s words found in Matthew 11:

10:08.938 --> 10:14.878 align:center line:79%
“Come unto me, all ye that labor and are
heavy laden, and I will give you rest.

10:15.078 --> 10:20.550 align:center line:79%
Take my yoke upon you, and learn of me;
for I am meek and lowly in heart:

10:20.550 --> 10:23.319 align:center line:81%
and ye shall find rest unto your souls.

10:23.319 --> 10:27.223 align:center line:79%
For my yoke is easy,
and my burden is light.”

10:27.457 --> 10:31.127 align:center line:79%
Just like those Saints in Africa,
I know this promise is true.

10:31.427 --> 10:34.063 align:center line:79%
It is true there,
and it is true everywhere.

10:34.297 --> 10:37.300 align:center line:79%
Of this I testify
in the name of Jesus Christ,

10:37.300 --> 10:38.301 align:center line:81%
amen.

